.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.PP
.nf
Responsible for evaluating links for a particular project\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS " None pip\&._internal\&.index\&.package_finder\&.LinkEvaluator\&.__init__ ( self, str project_name, str canonical_name, FrozenSet[str] formats, \fBTargetPython\fP target_python, bool allow_yanked, Optional[bool]  ignore_requires_python = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
:param project_name: The user supplied package name\&.
:param canonical_name: The canonical package name\&.
:param formats: The formats allowed for this package\&. Should be a set
    with 'binary' or 'source' or both in it\&.
:param target_python: The target Python interpreter to use when
    evaluating link compatibility\&. This is used, for example, to
    check wheel compatibility, as well as when checking the Python
    version, e\&.g\&. the Python version embedded in a link filename
    (or egg fragment) and against an HTML link's optional PEP 503
    'data-requires-python' attribute\&.
:param allow_yanked: Whether files marked as yanked (in the sense
    of PEP 592) are permitted to be candidates for install\&.
:param ignore_requires_python: Whether to ignore incompatible
    PEP 503 'data-requires-python' values in HTML links\&. Defaults
    to False\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS " Tuple[\fBLinkType\fP, str] pip\&._internal\&.index\&.package_finder\&.LinkEvaluator\&.evaluate_link ( self, \fBLink\fP link)"

.PP
.nf
Determine whether a link is a candidate for installation\&.

:return: A tuple (result, detail), where *result* is an enum
    representing whether the evaluation found a candidate, or the reason
    why one is not found\&. If a candidate is found, *detail* will be the
    candidate's version string; if one is not found, it contains the
    reason the link fails to qualify\&.

.fi
.PP
 
